body:
Fork synced at v0.18.0.

What changed: the global panic hook (`install_panic_hook`) is gone. On Windows, `main` wraps `camcraft_ui::run` in `catch_unwind` and shows the box only for a panic that escapes `run` (payload turned into text without panicking, exit code 101) or a non-zero exit with no console. A failed `CONOUT$` open after a successful `AttachConsole` now counts as no console. The payload-to-text function is in new `crates/ui/src/panic_text.rs` (not cfg(windows)). No new dependency, no unwrap/expect. Merged with #1287's code.

Pinning test: `panic_text::tests::payload_text_reads_str_string_and_other` (`cargo test -p camcraft-ui --bin camcraft-ui payload_text`).

Verification: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` green; clippy -D warnings on camcraft-ui bins clean; `win_console.rs` checked standalone with `rustc --target x86_64-pc-windows-gnu --emit=metadata` (no errors).

**Nothing was built or run on Windows.** The full crate was not compiled for Windows (no mingw C compiler on the build box); the `main.rs` Windows block was not compiled. Windows hand-checks:
- double-click start (box only on real start-up failure);
- start from a terminal (log visible, no box);
- redirect and pipe (`> log.txt 2>&1`, `| more`);
- a forced start-up failure by double-click (box shows once);
- a bad STEP import by double-click shows NO box.

Changelog: Windows: the start-up error box no longer pops for panics the app handles itself (#1325)
Effort: medium

Fixes #1325
